-"playwright" is default fixture, so you need not define it.
-headless=False -> headed mode....you can see what is going on the browser
-"page" fixture used chromium engine in headless mode by default. But when using this you can not do some customisations like switching between 2 contexts.
-CSS Selector: #id or .classname or tagname(not preferred since there are many tagnames in page)
-Keep imports absolute (never rely on relative .. imports in test suites).
-Run pytest from the project root or parent folder.
-Use pytest.ini or pyproject.toml to enforce consistent paths across local dev, PyCharm, and CI/CD.
-Keep __init__.py files empty unless you want to expose shortcuts.
-Put shared fixtures in conftest.py at the package root → pytest auto‑discovers them.
-Use session scope for static data (like credentials, configs).
-Keep fixtures modular: one fixture per responsibility (credentials, browser, API client, etc.).
-Avoid hard‑coding paths → always resolve relative to __file__.
-for multiproject setup:
    >One pytest.ini per project → isolates test discovery.
    >Run "pytest" command from project root or specify the project folder explicitly if running from parent folder(PycharmProjects).
    e.g. pytest PythonPlaywright
    >Use conftest.py per project for fixtures local to that project.
    >CI/CD pipelines run pytest per project, not globally.